/core/loop.ts (fixed timestep 60 Hz + interpolation), src/render/effects.ts (SkidMarks ring buffer with BufferAttribute.addUpdateRange partial uploads, custom ShaderMaterial; Smoke InstancedMesh), src/render/postfx.ts (radial blur pass into a HalfFloat WebGLRenderTarget, samples 0 on mobile), src/render/scene.ts (renderer, shadows, FollowCamera, shadow camera resized with zoom), src/render/world.ts (static meshes, InstancedMesh trees ~1300, road decals), src/render/carModel.ts, src/render/tuerca.ts, src/render/ambience.ts.\n\nFind, with concrete evidence (file:line and the exact failure scenario):\n- Correctness bugs that would make skid marks or smoke not render, render late, flicker, or disappear on iOS Safari / WebGL2 (e.g. updateRanges semantics in three r187, ring buffer wrap, alpha attribute, depth/polygonOffset/renderOrder/transparent sorting, frustum culling, HalfFloat render target or tone mapping/color space in the post pass, Math.random-based emission tied to frame rate, per-frame allocations).\n- Performance problems in the render loop on a mid-range phone: per-frame allocations (new Vector2 etc.), redundant matrix/attribute uploads, needsUpdate on whole buffers, shadow map cost (shadow camera size vs map size, castShadow on thousands of instances), overdraw, draw calls, the extra post pass, DOM updates in the HUD each frame, anything O(n) per frame over large arrays (e.g. road nearest-point search).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4c84466-785e-4e57-a4cb-68dd2a444b8d","uuid":"c5dc4d27-387c-4bec-99c0-5f51d2fa79cf","timestamp":"2026-11-01T13:20:09.264Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Sun Nov  1 14:20:09 CET 2026\nNov  1 14:20:08 2026 5339\n20062 /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/repo/.venv/bin/python .venv/bin/coverage run --source=taiga --omit=*tests*,*commands*,*migrations*,*admin*,*.jinja,*dashboard*,*settings*,*wsgi*,*questions*,*documents* -m pytest -v --tb=native --pythonwarnings=default --reuse-db\n2095