{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pm9EWWmaZ794kg3qQPJ5Kq","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/repo/.agents/skills/add-api-endpoint/SKILL.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4c84466-785e-4e57-a4cb-68dd2a444b8d","uuid":"0b26b81f-82d9-4a68-bd9b-4c8ef79e8408","timestamp":"2026-11-01T13:22:02.494Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/repo/.agents/skills/add-api-endpoint/SKILL.md","oldString":"Project resources use `HasProjectPerm(\"view_us\")` style checks; look at","newString":"Project resources use `HasProjectPerm(\"view_us\")` and `IsProjectAdmin()` from `taiga.permissions.permissions`; look at","originalFile":"---\nname: add-api-endpoint\ndescription: Use when you add a new REST resource or a new action to an existing viewset under /api/v1/ in taiga-back.\n---\n\n# Add an API endpoint\n\nReference example: `taiga/userstorage/` (small, complete) and its test `tests/integration/resources_permissions/test_storage_resources.py`.\n\n1. Model and migration (skip for an action on an existing model). Add the model to the app's `models.py`, then:\n   ```bash\n   DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE=tests.config .venv/bin/python manage.py makemigrations <app_label>\n   make migrations-check\n   ```\n   A new app must be added to `INSTALLED_APPS` in `settings/common.py`.\n\n2. Serializer and validator. Output goes in `serializers.py` (Taiga serializers, see the app neighbours), input checks in `validators.py` (`validator_class` on the viewset).\n\n3. Permissions in `permissions.py`: subclass `taiga.base.api.permissions.TaigaResourcePermission` and set one entry per action (`retrieve_perms`, `create_perms`, `update_perms`, `destroy_perms`, `list_perms`, or `enough_perms` / `global_perms`). Project resources use `HasProjectPerm(\"view_us\")` style checks; look at `taiga/projects/userstories/permissions.py`.\n\n4. Viewset in `api.py`: subclass a class from `taiga.base.api` (`ModelCrudViewSet`, `ModelListViewSet`, `GenericViewSet`). Set `model`, `serializer_class`, `validator_class`, `permission_classes`, `filter_backends`. Extra actions use `@list_route` / `@detail_route` from `taiga.base.decorators`. Raise errors from `taiga.base.exceptions` (`exc.BadRequest`, `exc.NotFound`, `exc.PermissionDenied`).\n\n5. Register the route in `taiga/routers.py`:\n   ```python\n   from taiga.<app>.api import <Name>ViewSet\n   router.register(r\"<prefix>\", <Name>ViewSet, base_name=\"<prefix>\")\n   ```\n   URL names follow `<base_name>-list` and `<base_name>-detail`.\n\n6. Tests:\n   - Behaviour: `tests/integration/test_<app>.py`, with `client.login(user)` and `reverse(\"<base_name>-list\")`.\n   - Permission matrix: `tests/integration/resources_permissions/test_<app>_resources.py` with `helper_test_http_method(client, \"get\", url, None, users)` and the expected status list for anonymous, non-member, member, admin.\n   - Factories: add one to `tests/factories.py` if the model is new.\n   ```bash\n   .venv/bin/pytest tests/integration/resources_permissions/test_<app>_resources.py --reuse-db\n   ```\n\n7. If the resource changes project data that others watch, check whether it needs history (`taiga/projects/history`), timeline (`taiga/timeline`), webhooks (`taiga/webhooks/signal_handlers.py`) or events (`taiga/events`). Follow how user stories do it.\n\n8. Run `make check-fast`, then the integration files you touched (or `make check`). Commit with `feat: ...`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":16,"oldLines":7,"newStart":16,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," 2. Serializer and validator. Output goes in `serializers.py` (Taiga serializers, see the app neighbours), input checks in `validators.py` (`validator_class` on the viewset)."," ","-3. Permissions in `permissions.py`: subclass `taiga.base.api.permissions.TaigaResourcePermission` and set one entry per action (`retrieve_perms`, `create_perms`, `update_perms`, `destroy_perms`, `list_perms`, or `enough_perms` / `global_perms`). Project resources use `HasProjectPerm(\"view_us\")` style checks; look at `taiga/projects/userstories/permissions.py`.","+3. Permissions in `permissions.py`: subclass `taiga.base.api.permissions.TaigaResourcePermission` and set one entry per action (`retrieve_perms`, `create_perms`, `update_perms`, `destroy_perms`, `list_perms`, or `enough_perms` / `global_perms`). Project resources use `HasProjectPerm(\"view_us\")` and `IsProjectAdmin()` from `taiga.permissions.permissions`; look at `taiga/projects/userstories/permissions.py`."," "," 4. Viewset in `api.py`: subclass a class from `taiga.base.api` (`ModelCrudViewSet`, `ModelListViewSet`, `GenericViewSet`). Set `model`, `serializer_class`, `validator_class`, `permission_classes`, `filter_backends`. Extra actions use `@list_route` / `@detail_route` from `taiga.base.decorators`. Raise errors from `taiga.base.exceptions` (`exc.BadRequest`, `exc.NotFound`, `exc.PermissionDenied`)."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pm9EWWmaZ794kg3qQPJ5Kq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
