{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jw2QnynWJ2mRyFZ3Deb5SV","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/repo/.agents/skills/debug-local/SKILL.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4c84466-785e-4e57-a4cb-68dd2a444b8d","uuid":"578a6374-ecc2-4fb0-8ed4-6a6b2eab74a3","timestamp":"2026-11-01T13:36:55.239Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/repo/.agents/skills/debug-local/SKILL.md","oldString":"   - If the test database looks broken after a migration change, run once without `--reuse-db` (or add `--create-db`).","newString":"   - `--reuse-db` keeps a database that transactional tests have flushed: rows from data migrations (for example the `is_system` users that `taiga/hooks` looks up) are gone. A `DoesNotExist` on data the test did not create usually means this: run again with `--create-db`.","originalFile":"---\nname: debug-local\ndescription: Use when a test fails, an API call returns an unexpected status, or behaviour differs from what you expect, and you need to reproduce and inspect it on your machine.\n---\n\n# Debug taiga-back locally\n\n1. Check the environment first:\n   ```bash\n   docker compose ps                 # postgres must be \"healthy\"\n   make db-up                        # starts it if needed\n   .venv/bin/python --version        # must be 3.10.x\n   ```\n   `password authentication failed for user \"taiga\"` means another PostgreSQL answers on port 5432 (see `docs/local-dev.md`, Common problems).\n\n2. Reproduce with the smallest test:\n   ```bash\n   .venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_slug.py -k <name> --reuse-db -x -vv --tb=long\n   ```\n   For an API bug, write a test in `tests/integration` with the `client` fixture from `tests/fixtures.py` and `tests/factories.py`; it is faster and more repeatable than clicking in a front end.\n\n3. Stop in the code:\n   ```bash\n   .venv/bin/pytest <test> --reuse-db --pdb      # debugger at the failure\n   .venv/bin/pytest <test> --reuse-db -s         # needed when you add breakpoint()\n   ```\n\n4. Reproduce against a running API when needed:\n   ```bash\n   make db-reset   # DESTROYS local data; loads admin/123123 and sample projects\n   make dev        # http://localhost:8000/api/v1/\n   curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\\n        -d '{\"type\": \"normal\", \"username\": \"admin\", \"password\": \"123123\"}'\n   ```\n   Use the returned `auth_token` as `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Logs of the `taiga` logger print in the `make dev` terminal (`LOGGING` in `settings/common.py`).\n\n5. Inspect data:\n   ```bash\n   .venv/bin/python manage.py shell\n   docker compose exec postgres psql -U taiga taiga        # dev database\n   docker compose exec postgres psql -U taiga test_taiga   # test database kept by --reuse-db\n   ```\n\n6. Known traps:\n   - Tests run with `CELERY_ENABLED = False` and eager tasks; a bug that only happens in the worker needs `make worker` and RabbitMQ (`docker compose --profile async up -d`).\n   - Many resource-permission tests call `disconnect_signals()`; history, timeline and notifications are then not created.\n   - Throttling is disabled in `tests/config.py` but active in `make dev`.\n   - If the test database looks broken after a migration change, run once without `--reuse-db` (or add `--create-db`).\n\n7. When fixed, follow the `implement-change` skill from step 5 (migrations, `make check-fast`, log entry).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":45,"oldLines":6,"newStart":45,"newLines":6,"lines":["    - Tests run with `CELERY_ENABLED = False` and eager tasks; a bug that only happens in the worker needs `make worker` and RabbitMQ (`docker compose --profile async up -d`).","    - Many resource-permission tests call `disconnect_signals()`; history, timeline and notifications are then not created.","    - Throttling is disabled in `tests/config.py` but active in `make dev`.","-   - If the test database looks broken after a migration change, run once without `--reuse-db` (or add `--create-db`).","+   - `--reuse-db` keeps a database that transactional tests have flushed: rows from data migrations (for example the `is_system` users that `taiga/hooks` looks up) are gone. A `DoesNotExist` on data the test did not create usually means this: run again with `--create-db`."," "," 7. When fixed, follow the `implement-change` skill from step 5 (migrations, `make check-fast`, log entry)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Jw2QnynWJ2mRyFZ3Deb5SV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
