{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019MXcgFAPubSpoJYQDWvJwG","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/repo/docs/harness/log.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4c84466-785e-4e57-a4cb-68dd2a444b8d","uuid":"0a681204-6e60-46d0-94f1-3d85e5200444","timestamp":"2026-11-01T13:36:57.594Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/Users/victor/Repos/unwritten/uw-harness-cases/taiga/repo/docs/harness/log.md","oldString":"- **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage.","newString":"- **The full gate needs a fresh test database.** A first `make check` with `--reuse-db` had 51 failures in `tests/integration/test_hooks_*`: transactional tests had flushed the reused database, so the system users created by a data migration were missing. `make check` and `make test` now use `--create-db`, like CI. The fast gate keeps `--reuse-db` (unit tests do not need that data).\n- **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage in about 15 minutes on a laptop.","originalFile":"# Harness log\n\nOne entry per significant change: date, what changed, what was learned, what is left.\n\n## Notes from the harness build\n\n- **Lint is limited in the gates.** `flake8 .` with the `setup.cfg` rules reports 1309 violations in existing code (top codes: F401 163, E501 118, E402 118, E231 84, E252 78). CI never ran flake8 before. The gates run `flake8 --select=E9,F63,F7 .` (syntax errors and invalid comparisons), which passes. `make lint-full` runs the full rules. No rule was added to the flake8 configuration.\n- **Undefined names (F821) in product code, left for a human.** `taiga/projects/userstories/filters.py:45-47` uses `logger` and `exc` without importing them: `UserStoryStatusesFilter` raises `NameError` instead of `BadRequest` for a non-integer `project` parameter. On `GET /api/v1/userstories` the bug is masked because `CanViewUsFilterBackend` runs first and already returns 400, so it is latent. `taiga/base/fields.py:111-133` uses `ValidationError` and `NestedValidationError` without importing them. `taiga/projects/attachments/services.py:95` uses string type hints for models that are not imported (no runtime effect). `taiga/events/middleware.py` has three unused `global _local` statements (F824).\n- **Unit tests are the fast gate.** `make check-fast` runs `tests/unit` (238 tests, about 30 s with a warm test database). Integration tests run only in `make check`.\n- **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage. Most time is in fixture setup: `tests/factories.py` hashes a password for each user with PBKDF2 (`PASSWORD_HASHERS` in `settings/common.py`). A faster hasher in `tests/config.py` would speed it up, but it changes test settings and needs a team decision.\n- **Tests need PostgreSQL.** The gates start it with `docker compose up -d --wait postgres` (`make db-up`) unless `CI` is set. The compose service runs with `fsync=off`; without it, the first test run took about 100 s for the unit tests alone on Docker for Mac.\n- **Git hook.** The sandbox did not allow writing `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, so the pre-push hook is `.githooks/pre-push`, installed with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` by `make setup`.\n- **CI.** `.github/workflows/tests-and-coverall.yml` now runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` (setup, check-fast, check) instead of calling pytest directly. `make check` keeps the same coverage command, so the Coveralls step still finds `.coverage`. The unit tests run twice in CI (fast gate, then full gate).\n- **Dev dependency added.** `flake8` in `requirements-devel.in`; `requirements-devel.txt` regenerated with `pip-compile` without `--upgrade` (only additions: flake8, mccabe, pycodestyle, pyflakes).\n- **Secret in tracked code, not changed.** `settings/common.py:249` holds a hard-coded `SECRET_KEY`. See the TODO in `AGENTS.md` and the `blocked` list of the harness build.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":7,"oldLines":7,"newStart":7,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - **Lint is limited in the gates.** `flake8 .` with the `setup.cfg` rules reports 1309 violations in existing code (top codes: F401 163, E501 118, E402 118, E231 84, E252 78). CI never ran flake8 before. The gates run `flake8 --select=E9,F63,F7 .` (syntax errors and invalid comparisons), which passes. `make lint-full` runs the full rules. No rule was added to the flake8 configuration."," - **Undefined names (F821) in product code, left for a human.** `taiga/projects/userstories/filters.py:45-47` uses `logger` and `exc` without importing them: `UserStoryStatusesFilter` raises `NameError` instead of `BadRequest` for a non-integer `project` parameter. On `GET /api/v1/userstories` the bug is masked because `CanViewUsFilterBackend` runs first and already returns 400, so it is latent. `taiga/base/fields.py:111-133` uses `ValidationError` and `NestedValidationError` without importing them. `taiga/projects/attachments/services.py:95` uses string type hints for models that are not imported (no runtime effect). `taiga/events/middleware.py` has three unused `global _local` statements (F824)."," - **Unit tests are the fast gate.** `make check-fast` runs `tests/unit` (238 tests, about 30 s with a warm test database). Integration tests run only in `make check`.","-- **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage. Most time is in fixture setup: `tests/factories.py` hashes a password for each user with PBKDF2 (`PASSWORD_HASHERS` in `settings/common.py`). A faster hasher in `tests/config.py` would speed it up, but it changes test settings and needs a team decision.","+- **The full gate needs a fresh test database.** A first `make check` with `--reuse-db` had 51 failures in `tests/integration/test_hooks_*`: transactional tests had flushed the reused database, so the system users created by a data migration were missing. `make check` and `make test` now use `--create-db`, like CI. The fast gate keeps `--reuse-db` (unit tests do not need that data).","+- **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage in about 15 minutes on a laptop. Most time is in fixture setup: `tests/factories.py` hashes a password for each user with PBKDF2 (`PASSWORD_HASHERS` in `settings/common.py`). A faster hasher in `tests/config.py` would speed it up, but it changes test settings and needs a team decision."," - **Tests need PostgreSQL.** The gates start it with `docker compose up -d --wait postgres` (`make db-up`) unless `CI` is set. The compose service runs with `fsync=off`; without it, the first test run took about 100 s for the unit tests alone on Docker for Mac."," - **Git hook.** The sandbox did not allow writing `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, so the pre-push hook is `.githooks/pre-push`, installed with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` by `make setup`."," - **CI.** `.github/workflows/tests-and-coverall.yml` now runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` (setup, check-fast, check) instead of calling pytest directly. `make check` keeps the same coverage command, so the Coveralls step still finds `.coverage`. The unit tests run twice in CI (fast gate, then full gate)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019MXcgFAPubSpoJYQDWvJwG","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
