es.py:95` uses string type hints for models that are not imported (no runtime effect). `taiga/events/middleware.py` has three unused `global _local` statements (F824).\n- **Unit tests are the fast gate.** `make check-fast` runs `tests/unit` (238 tests, about 30 s with a warm test database). Integration tests run only in `make check`.\n- **The full gate needs a fresh test database.** A first `make check` with `--reuse-db` had 51 failures in `tests/integration/test_hooks_*`: transactional tests had flushed the reused database, so the system users created by a data migration were missing. `make check` and `make test` now use `--create-db`, like CI. The fast gate keeps `--reuse-db` (unit tests do not need that data).\n- **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage in about 15 minutes on a laptop. Most time is in fixture setup: `tests/factories.py` hashes a password for each user with PBKDF2 (`PASSWORD_HASHERS` in `settings/common.py`). A faster hasher in `tests/config.py` would speed it up, but it changes test settings and needs a team decision.\n- **Tests need PostgreSQL.** The gates start it with `docker compose up -d --wait postgres` (`make db-up`) unless `CI` is set. The compose service runs with `fsync=off`; without it, the first test run took about 100 s for the unit tests alone on Docker for Mac.\n- **Git hook.** The sandbox did not allow writing `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, so the pre-push hook is `.githooks/pre-push`, installed with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` by `make setup`.\n- **CI.** `.github/workflows/tests-and-coverall.yml` now runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` (setup, check-fast, check) instead of calling pytest directly. `make check` keeps the same coverage command, so the Coveralls step still finds `.coverage`. The unit tests run twice in CI (fast gate, then full gate).\n- **Dev dependency added.** `flake8` in `requirements-devel.in`; `requirements-devel.txt` regenerated with `pip-compile` without `--upgrade` (only additions: flake8, mccabe, pycodestyle, pyflakes).\n- **Secret in tracked code, not changed.** `settings/common.py:249` holds a hard-coded `SECRET_KEY`. See the TODO in `AGENTS.md` and the `blocked` list of the harness build.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":6,"newStart":11,"newLines":6,"lines":[" - **The full suite is slow.** `make check` runs all 1751 collected tests with coverage in about 15 minutes on a laptop. Most time is in fixture setup: `tests/factories.py` hashes a password for each user with PBKDF2 (`PASSWORD_HASHERS` in `settings/common.py`). A faster hasher in `tests/config.py` would speed it up, but it changes test settings and needs a team decision."," - **Tests need PostgreSQL.** The gates start it with `docker compose up -d --wait postgres` (`make db-up`) unless `CI` is set. The compose service runs with `fsync=off`; without it, the first test run took about 100 s for the unit tests alone on Docker for Mac."," - **Git hook.** The sandbox did not allow writing `.pre-commit-config.yaml`, so the pre-push hook is `.githooks/pre-push`, installed with `git config core.hooksPath .githooks` by `make setup`.","-- **CI.** `.github/workflows/tests-and-coverall.yml` now runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` (setup, check-fast, check) instead of calling pytest directly. `make check` keeps the same coverage command, so the Coveralls step still finds `.coverage`. The unit tests run twice in CI (fast gate, then full gate).","+- **CI.** `.github/workflows/tests-and-coverall.yml` now runs `npx -y uw-harness verify` (setup, check-fast, check) instead of calling pytest directly. `make check` keeps the same coverage command, so the Coveralls step still finds `.coverage`. The unit tests run twice in CI (fast gate, then full gate). On 2026-11-01 `npx -y uw-harness` returned 404 from the npm registry: the CI step fails until the package is published (or the step is changed to call `make check` directly)."," - **Dev dependency added.** `flake8` in `require